markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Analyzing the Algorithm</h1>
<img src="https://images.code.org/8c57754f154962c0619e3596f0f849e8-image-1741713107783.png" alt="Icon representing an algorithm with a settings gear" style="border-radius:10px; float: left; height: 125px; margin: 0px 20px 10px 0px;">
<p>Now that we've explored how algorithms impact our daily lives and the ethical concerns they raise, it's time to put that knowledge into practice.</p>
<p>In this <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zCe5nxpYzzU7C9rF-D9rqVfpgwgSzOcjShuh2UpeWuw/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="font-weight: bold;">activity</a>, you'll examine a flawed music recommendation algorithm and consider ways to make it more fair and inclusive.</p>
<div style="clear:both;"></div>

<h2>Activity: Fixing a Biased Music Algorithm</h2>

<h3><b>Step 1: Review the Algorithm</b></h3>

<div style="float:right; width:420px; margin: 4px 0 16px 24px;">
  <p style="text-align:center; font-weight:bold; color:#4C42CF; margin-bottom: 6px;">Song Recommendation Flow</p>
  <div style="width:420px; height:390px; overflow:hidden;">
    <div role="group" aria-label="Song recommendation flowchart. The user selects a song. The program stores the song's genre and recommends another song from that genre. The program asks if the user liked the song. If yes, it recommends another song from the same genre. If no, it recommends a random song from the same genre. Both paths loop back to the decision." style="position:relative; width:700px; height:650px; transform: scale(0.6); transform-origin: top left; background-color:#FFFFFF; border:1px solid #E4E2F8; border-radius:12px; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">

