      </div>
    <span style="position:absolute; left:220px; top:302px; background-color:#CCF1D0; color:#000000; border:2px solid #34BD43; border-radius:14px; padding:2px 9px; font-size:15px; font-weight:bold; z-index:3;">Yes</span>
      <span style="position:absolute; left:455px; top:302px; background-color:#CCF1D0; color:#000000; border:2px solid #34BD43; border-radius:14px; padding:2px 9px; font-size:15px; font-weight:bold; z-index:3;">No</span>
    <div style="position:absolute; left:55px; top:430px; width:260px; height:80px; box-sizing:border-box; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; text-align:center; background-color:#D5EFFF; color:#000000; border:4px solid #0099F3; border-radius:5px; padding:10px; font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; line-height:1.3; z-index:2;">
        Recommend another song<br>from the same genre
      </div>
    <div style="position:absolute; left:385px; top:430px; width:260px; height:80px; box-sizing:border-box; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; text-align:center; background-color:#D5EFFF; color:#000000; border:4px solid #0099F3; border-radius:5px; padding:10px; font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; line-height:1.3; z-index:2;">
        Recommend a random song<br>from the same genre
      </div>
    <div style="position:absolute; left:250px; top:570px; width:200px; height:55px; box-sizing:border-box; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; text-align:center; background-color:#D5EFFF; color:#000000; border:4px solid #0099F3; border-radius:5px; padding:8px; font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; z-index:2;">
        Loop back to the decision
      </div>

   </div>
  </div>
</div>

<p>Take a look at the flowchart to the right. This represents a music recommendation algorithm that suggests songs to a user based on their first song choice.</p>

<p><b>Ask yourself:</b></p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• How does the algorithm make decisions?</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• What patterns do you notice in how songs are recommended?</p>


<h3><b>Step 2: Identify the Problem</b></h3>
<p>Think critically about the limitations of this algorithm. <b>Consider:</b></p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Does this recommendation system encourage variety, or does it keep users within a narrow selection of songs?</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• How might this impact users who want to discover new music?</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• Are there any unintended biases in how it selects songs?</p>

<h3><b>Step 3: Propose Improvements</b></h3>
<p>Now, redesign the algorithm!</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• What changes could you make to ensure a more diverse set of recommendations?</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• How could user preferences or feedback be incorporated?</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• How might your improvements create a better experience for a wider range of users?</p>

<h2>Reflection</h2>
<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px 20px; width: 90%; margin: 16px auto;">
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Can you think of any real-world examples where biased algorithms affect what people see, buy, or experience?</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• How can we help students recognize and question biased algorithms in their own lives?</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• What ethical challenges do we face when trying to make algorithm-based decisions fair?</p>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 16px 0;">
